    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the trip facts that can be read are read, but the one fact that decides the money cannot be read on this record, so this case goes to a human reviewer. No refund is issued and no charge is restored while that happens; the 14.05 SGD metered fare is held.\n\nWhat I accepted. The route taken is settled by the platform trip record and the driver-device trace together (EV-TRIP-05009, EV-GPS-05009): the vehicle left the recommended BKE route at Woodlands Avenue 2, went by Woodlands Road and Bukit Panjang Road, and rejoined at Petir Road. Measured POL-RD-22's way, from the platform's recorded distances, the deviation is 10.0 km - 8.5 km = 1.50 km, over POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance, and POL-RD-22 says the trace is not used to re-measure it. The driver's in-app message at 15:49:39 and the rider's 'ok can' at 15:49:59 satisfy POL-RD-21's notice and acknowledgment: EV-CHAT-05009 is complete at weight 1.0, and the notice came before the deviation the platform logged at 15:51:59. So the driver is right that this was an announced, accepted reroute, and the rider is right that the notification and agreement alone do not decide the money.\n\nWhat decides the case, and why it is not decidable here. POL-RD-24's matrix turns on whether the reroute was traffic-justified, and POL-RD-23 permits that finding only on traffic data for the recommended route at the trip time - a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY intersecting the route and the trip window - not on a driver's assertion. That artifact, EV-ADVIS-05009-01, is MISSING: weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, because the platform's request to the LTA feed timed out and was never retried. The record is silent on traffic, and the pre-pass itself notes that this silence is not a finding that the BKE was clear. The traffic limb therefore has nothing to read: it is undecided, and an undecided limb supports neither the driver's no-refund (POL-RD-24 row (a) needs traffic justification to hold) nor the rider's refund (row (d) needs traffic justification to fail). POL-GEN-26 requires escalation for exactly this situation - 'whether traffic justified the reroute' is one of the facts it names - where the evidence that would carry it is missing. The rider's 'I could not find any accident news' does not fill that gap either: a later search is not a finding about traffic that afternoon.\n\nOn the arithmetic. Both sides put the excess distance fare at 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.08 SGD, without surge (POL-RD-24; EV-FARE-05009). That figure is right and the rider is right that no row returns the whole 3.50 SGD asked for and no more than 1.08 SGD is ever available under this clause; the ledger also confirms nothing has yet been returned (refund_issued_sgd 0.00, payment_status CHARGED). But 1.08 SGD is payable only if a row of the matrix can be selected, and on this record none can. So nothing is paid and nothing is restored at this stage.\n\nConfidence. My confidence cannot exceed the evidence that carries the deciding fact: the only artifact able to carry the traffic-justification finding is EV-ADVIS-05009-01 at weight 0.0 (MISSING_ARTIFACT), so the cap is 0.0. That is below the 0.80 that POL-RD-25 requires for an AI ruling on a route deviation, which is a second, independent reason the case escalates. Both profiles show fraud_flags 0, so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 threshold does not apply; the contested 3.50 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, though POL-RD-25's 0.80 bar for route deviations applies whatever the value; and POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is switched off (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false) and would be met at 1.50 km in any case.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer, who has the means to retrieve the feed: was the recommended BKE route congested, blocked or the scene of an incident between about 15:51 and 16:03 on 2026-08-23? If the LTA data shows yes, POL-RD-24 row (a) gives no refund; if it shows no, row (d) gives a 1.08 SGD refund. No referral is added: the route-deviation policy contains no referral clause, and the goodwill and fee-check referrals belong to other categories."
  },
